-- title:
--   Global frames for the cube of an effective line bundle
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and let $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be a morphism of schemes (in universe $0$) equipped with: a relative group law $L$ on $f$, i.e. functorial multiplication, unit and inverse operations on the sets $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ of $T$-points over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, satisfying associativity, the unit and inverse laws and compatibility with base change in $T$; a hypothesis $hc$ that $L$ is commutative; and the property bundle `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` asserting that $f$ is smooth, proper, has connected fibres and admits some relative group law. Let $\mathcal M$ be a module on $A$ which is invertible, i.e. every point of $A$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ on which the pullback of $\mathcal M$ along $U \hookrightarrow A$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of rings-modules of $U$. Assume that, for the $k$-algebra structure on $\Gamma(A,\top)$ induced by $f$ and the resulting $k$-module structure on $\Gamma(\mathcal M,\top)$, one has $\operatorname{finrank}_k \Gamma(\mathcal M, \top) > 0$. Let $\mathcal N$ be a module on $A$ together with an isomorphism $\mathcal N \cong \mathcal M \otimes \mathcal M \otimes \mathcal M$. Then there exist $N \in \mathbb N$, global sections $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_N \in \Gamma(\mathcal N, \top)$ and opens $U_0,\dots,U_N$ of $A$ with $\bigvee_i U_i = \top$ such that each $\sigma_i$ is a frame on $U_i$: for every open $W \le U_i$, the map $\Gamma(A,W) \to \Gamma(\mathcal N, W)$, $g \mapsto g \cdot (\sigma_i|_W)$, is bijective.
--
--   This is the first step of Lefschetz's theorem for abelian varieties: if $\mathcal M$ is an invertible sheaf with a nonzero global section, then $\mathcal M^{\otimes 3}$ is generated by its global sections, here in the explicit form of finitely many global sections each framing $\mathcal N$ on a member of an open cover. It feeds the construction of polarisations and is cited by the corresponding statement phrased with a tensor power, [`AlgebraicGeometry.Polarisation.exists_isFrameOn_iSup_eq_top_of_iso_tensorPow_of_finrank_pos`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Polarisation.exists_isFrameOn_iSup_eq_top_of_iso_tensorPow_of_finrank_pos).
